<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A boda boda rides along a straight road through a junction <m>J</m>. Take its direction of travel as positive. Its velocity at time <m>t</m> seconds is <m>v = {-\frac{3 t^2}{10}+3 t+8}</m> m/s, for <m>0 \le t \le {5}</m>. When <m>t = 0</m> its displacement from <m>J</m> is <m>{-20}</m> m (negative: it has not yet reached <m>J</m>). Give exact values.</p><p>(a) Find its acceleration when <m>t = {3}</m>.</p><div><m>a =</m> <fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/> m/s<m>^2</m>  </div><p>(b) Find its displacement from its starting point at <m>t = {5}</m>, that is, how far it moves between <m>t = 0</m> and <m>t = {5}</m>.</p><div>Displacement <m>=</m> <fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/> m  </div><p>(c) Find its displacement from <m>J</m> when <m>t = {5}</m>.</p><div><m>s =</m> <fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/> m  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Differentiate the velocity to find the acceleration; integrate it to find the displacement.</p><p>(a) <m>a = \dfrac{dv}{dt} = {3-\frac{3 t}{5}}</m>, so at <m>t = {3}</m>, <m>a = {\frac{6}{5}}</m> m/s<m>^2</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>\displaystyle\int_0^{ {5} } \left({-\frac{3 t^2}{10}+3 t+8}\right)dt = \left[{-\frac{t^3}{10}+\frac{3 t^2}{2}+8 t}\right]_0^{ {5} } = {65}</m> m. The velocity is positive throughout, so the boda boda moves the same way all the time.</p><p>(c) Its displacement from <m>J</m> at the start was <m>{-20}</m> m, so at <m>t = {5}</m> it is <m>{-20} + {65} = {45}</m> m: it is now <m>{45}</m> m past <m>J</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{6}{5}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>65</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>45</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>